Howdy, Howdy, fellow Hackers,
   I've been enjoying NetHack for some time now (v 3.09), and I'm
fairly content that I've got a lot of the nuances and tricks to the
game nailed down. However, I have two problems that have repeatedly
proven to be rather disheartening, and perhaps someone can explain the
solutions to me.
(1) Is there a way to get a Bag of Holding to work properly? I know
that one can obtain one in either blessed or unblessed condition in a
number of permutations: bless/unbless while it is empty/full, or
create one (empty) in either blessed/unblessed condition on a
polypile. I haven't quite been able to tell *definitively*, but I
could swear that different things happen when you drop/pick up the
bag, or loot it while it's on the floor, or put items into it that
weren't there when it was blessed, etc. - some of this may be my
imagination, of course. My documentation insists that one should not
bless a bag *while* it is full, but I'm quite convinced that blessing
one while empty *still* fails to give a bag that works properly. Is it
possible that there is a limit to the weight/number of items that a
bag will carry without becoming heavier? I mean, ideally, a Bag should
never exceed a weight of 3, but I've never had one that worked that
way. I consider this a *major* hassle, and welcome any definitive
suggestions on the topic.
(2) I've noticed that when I use a Wish to obtain an artifact, I don't
seem to get one with its special properties intact: I wished for "a
blessed +3 war hammer named Mjollnir" and *got* one, but it does not
do any shock damage, ever, and I wished for "a blessed +3 long sword
named Excalibur" and got one, but it does not defend me against level
drains (as far as I can tell), and it most *certainly* does not
"search" like a ring of searching does. Anyone who can explain to me
what the problem is, or ways to consistently obtain *functional*
artifacts? I mean, what Excalibur does for me, as far as I can tell,
is nothing I couldn't do with *any* blessed +3 long sword, named or
otherwise. This doesn't make any sense to me.
   Any help, posted or mailed to me, would be much appreciated.
